WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.986
A5 happens in one change window,
because an S P N left on the old account

2
00:00:04.986 --> 00:00:09.663
while the service runs as the G M
S A breaks Kerberos to the service.

3
00:00:09.663 --> 00:00:12.649
Each S P N must have exactly one owner.

4
00:00:12.649 --> 00:00:18.800
Remove it from the old account, add it to
the G M S A, and list it with set S P N.

5
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.788
Then change the workload's identity.

6
00:00:20.788 --> 00:00:23.646
A G M S A logs on with a blank password,

7
00:00:23.646 --> 00:00:27.588
which Windows fills in, as
Learn's Entra page says.

8
00:00:27.588 --> 00:00:30.764
For a Windows service, S
C config sets the account,

9
00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:33.862
and the managed-account
query must report true.

10
00:00:33.862 --> 00:00:37.978
A scheduled task gets a new principal
with the password logon type,

11
00:00:37.978 --> 00:00:41.420
as Learn's assessment pages do
it, and an I I S application

12
00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.787
pool gets identity type three
with the blank password.

13
00:00:44.787 --> 00:00:47.740
The guide notes that
Learn has no single page

14
00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:50.613
showing that last one
end to end, so verify it.

15
00:00:50.613 --> 00:00:54.088
A6 is the thirty-day parallel
run: test end to end,

16
00:00:54.088 --> 00:00:58.099
keep the old account enabled,
and watch its logons stop.

17
00:00:58.099 --> 00:01:03.788
A7 disables the old account; deletion comes
later, through the decommission process.

18
00:01:03.788 --> 00:01:07.103
To roll back, switch the
workload back with the old

19
00:01:07.103 --> 00:01:10.220
password from the vault,
and move the S P Ns back.
